-- A NAMED-FIELD VARIANT whose CONSTRUCTOR is spelled `Plain` — the same registry
-- key `plainlib`'s record `Plain` uses, but owned by type `Holder`.  That is what
-- makes key `Plain` collided in `universeRecordIdentsRef` with two candidates
-- whose OWNING TYPE NAMES differ, so a match test that compares NEITHER half
-- ("first candidate wins") cannot tell them apart.
--
-- 🚨 AN EARLIER VERSION OF THIS HEADER SAID "an identity test that compares only
-- the declaring module (or only the key) cannot tell them apart."  THE FIRST HALF
-- IS FALSE, MEASURED: module-only tells them apart here correctly, and reds
-- nothing anywhere in the tree.  See `recordCandIsType`.
--
-- `hxOf` projects `hx` HERE, inside the declaring module, so this cell grades the
-- own-module route.  The `entry` route (receiver head `Holder`, arm (a) misses,
-- the field→owners path answers) was #1383: it was refused through the bare-key
-- `pairRecordByName "Plain"`, and is now answered from the identity companion.
-- That route is graded by
-- `test/llvm_fixtures_modules/record_variant_ctor_vs_xmod_record_type/`.
--
-- 🚨 AND THE RESIDUAL IS NOT ONLY THE LOUD REJECT.  An earlier version of this
-- header named only #1383 (S1, a false REJECT), which understates it: the SAME
-- `pairRecordByName (headL owners)` fallback also has a SILENT BUILT-BINARY face,
-- and that one is **#1216 (S0, OPEN)**.  Measured 2026-08-08: two modules each
-- declaring a named-field variant spelled `Cfg` whose owning types are `WrapA` and
-- `WrapZ`, same two `Int` fields at opposite indices, every projection inside its
-- own declaring module — `check` exits 0, `medaka run` prints the correct
-- `11,22,44,33`, and the BUILT BINARY prints `11,22,33,44` at exit 0 with no
-- diagnostic.  Neither key suffix-matches the other's head, so #1395's narrowing
-- never runs and the owners fallback picks by module-NAME sort order.  The full
-- repro is ported into
-- `test/must_fail_fixtures/1216-xmod-record-field-name-collision/claim.txt`
-- (one row per issue, so it could not have its own).  **Grade this residual
-- S0-silent, not only S1-loud** — that is the fact a reader weighing the
-- accept-widening above actually needs.
public export data Holder =
  | Plain { hx : Int }

export mkH : Holder
mkH = Plain { hx = 100 }

export hxOf : Holder -> Int
hxOf h = h.hx
